  "created": "2018-09-10T00:01:13.755Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Prior to the new update, the aural environment of the old loading screen was excellent. The ambient noise acted as a succinct audio cue for when you were loading, and when you were done, while not getting in the way. This was great for taking a moment to do other things or play other music, which is very easy to do with the Oculus Dash. \n\nNow, the screen blasts loud music at you. Because the menu is (still) inaccessible in loading screens, there's no way to turn it down short of muting VRChat in Windows - which is pretty annoying to do every time you move to a new world, removes the ability to hear when you've left, and is generally a bad user experience. \n\nThe option to remove it would be appreciated.",
